SUMMARY:Room 861 At Goodnights: Conor Janda
LOCATION:Goodnights Comedy Club\, 401 Woodburn Rd.\, Raleigh
DESCRIPTION:Conor Janda is a stand-up\, writer\, and actor. His writing exe
 mplifies both the neuroses of a New York transplant and the fiery spirit of
  a Philadelphia native. Conor was recently named a New Face of Comedy at th
 e Just for Laughs Festival in Montreal. He has been featured as a writer an
 d actor on the Gag\, Comedy Central’s queer digital channel.\n\nConor’s
  stand up covers everything from having a stay at home dad to going to an a
 ll boys Catholic school to getting sober from alcohol. He is too anxious to
  be at a Fire Island Underwear Party or a Philadelphia Eagles tailgate\, wh
 ich may be the only thing bridging those communities\, a glimmer of unity i
 n these divided times that Conor is happy to provide.\n\nWhen he’s not to
 uring around the country\, Conor is the co-creator\, writer\, and star of w
 eb series BOYS CLUB with friend and collaborator Nico Carney\, which can an
 d should be watched on YouTube. BOYS CLUB was originally developed as a ser
 ies with Imagine Entertainment and Scott King. One time\, someone kind of f
 amous said he was too kind to be as funny as he is.\n\nManagement reserves 
 the right to prevent customers from entering the facility who they deem dis
 ruptive or dangerous to other patrons.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/
 comedy-atlas/event/room-861-at-goodnights-conor-janda-20957/
